.1,\n        \"permutation\": 0.05,\n        \"replay\": 0.05\n      },\n      \"utility\": \"1-min(10,max(-10,estimate-true_gate))**2/100; noise scale=1\",\n      \"rmse\": \"sqrt(mean(clipped_error**2 over seeds)) then equal cases/families\",\n      \"bias\": \"abs(mean(signed clipped_error over seeds)) then equal cases/families; incomplete case contributes 10\",\n      \"failure\": {\n        \"utility\": 0,\n        \"signed_error\": 10,\n        \"squared_error\": 100,\n        \"control_success\": 0\n      },\n      \"control_metric_weights\": {\n        \"constant\": 0.5,\n        \"permutation\": 0.25,\n        \"replay\": 0.25\n      },\n      \"evidence_seed_score\": \"same hierarchy within seed, common sole replay contribution .05 shared across seed records; mean seed scores equals combined_score\",\n      \"failure_denominator\": \"161 search, 625 final, 5 smoke; unsuccessful matched controls count as failed episodes\"\n    },\n    \"time_plan\": {\n      \"wall_seconds\": 7200,\n      \"startup_allowance_seconds\": 180,\n      \"finish_reserve_seconds\": 30,\n      \"reset_timeout_seconds\": 1.0,\n      \"episode_overhead_seconds\": 2.7,\n      \"cleanup_derivation\": \"Candidate terminate .1 + kill/reap .2 + stderr reader reserve 1.0 =1.3; baseline same 1.3; bookkeeping .1 =2.7. Reader actually closes within .4, leaving conservative headroom; no repeated waits after reaping.\",\n      \"matched_work_seconds_per_method\": 1.2,\n      \"methods\": 6,\n      \"method_bookkeeping_seconds\": 0.01,\n      \"productive_time_floor\": null,\n      \"calibration\": \"No canonical productive-work minimum or threshold delegation exists. Work allowances bound actual fixed dimensions; do not sleep, inflate runtime or tune scientific thresholds.\",\n      \"platform\": \"Linux x86_64, CPython 3.11 or 3.12; native smoke needs Landlock ABI>=3 and libseccomp.so.2; no namespace privilege required. All numerical-library threads one, at most two cores per role; 8 GiB per role; no GPUs. Harness enforces production role CPU/memory isolation.\"\n    },\n    \"attribution\": \"Stanford3: Rossi & Ahmed (AAAI 2015), Traud, Mucha & Porter (Physica A 2012). Network Repository CC BY-SA as verified in canonical task; version not specified. Retain attribution and share-alike obligations. Archive checksum and 11586/568309 dimensions verified; no SNAP acquisition or restricted literature access.\"\n  }\n}\n{\n  \"schema_version\": 1,\n  \"canonical_task\": {\n    \"path\": \"task.md\",\n    \"sha256\": \"f03632993af2bfa32b3665a33757eb56790b5f90f43c715d596d1628531d1184\"\n  },\n  \"method\": {\n    \"class\": \"exposure_regression_gate\",\n    \"description\": \"Study when a fitted regression, evaluated at all-treated and all-control assignments, estimates finite-population GATE accurately. The candidate direction is ridge regression with an unpenalized intercept, own treatment, covariates, one-hop treated-neighbor fraction, fixed hinge bases and treatment-exposure interactions. Compare it with difference-in-means, own-treatment regression and linear one-hop regression. Test whether exposure adequacy, support near the endpoint interventions, interference strength and graph structure explain changes in bias and RMSE. Explicitly include misspecified two-hop interference, nonlinear interference and cluster assignment. This is a bounded simulation and semi-synthetic study, not a claim of universal superiority, identification under arbitrary interference, or novelty of regression adjustment itself. Favorable, unfavorable and inconclusive comparisons are all legitimate outcomes; publication requires uncertainty and limitations, not a positive effect. Search correctness means scientific-evaluation integrity and matched behavioral controls, not superiority. Final correctness independently means completed sealed integrity/control checks, not automatic publication. Fixed inputs, DGPs, score weights, finite penalties, explicit RPC operation counts and timing reservations are recorded in own-plane manifests. No feedback-dependence or changed-state gate applies to this nonadaptive regression task.\"\n  },\n  \"candidate\": {\n    \"interface\": \"python_rpc_v1:handle\",\n    \"editable_paths\": [\n      \"program_0/src\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"evaluators\": {\n    \"search\": \"evaluate.py\",\n    \"final\": \"evaluate_final.py\"\n  },\n  \"resources\": {\n    \"search_root\": \"resources/search\",\n    \"final_root\": \"resources/final\",\n    \"public_artifact_bundle\": null\n  },\n  \"data\": {\n    \"search_roles\": [\n      \"search_evaluation_plan\"\n    ],\n    \"final_roles\": [\n      \"final_evaluation_plan\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"metrics\": {\n    \"search\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"combined_score\",\n        \"data_role\": \"search_evaluation_plan\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"mean_capped_normalized_rmse\",\n        \"data_role\": \"search_evaluation_plan\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"mean_absolute_capped_normalized_bias\",\n        \"data_role\": \"search_evaluation_plan\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"failed_episode_fraction\",\n        \"data_role\": \"search_evaluation_plan\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"control_success_fraction\",\n        \"data_role\": \"search_evaluation_plan\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"final\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"combined_score\",\n        \"data_role\": \"final_evaluation_plan\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"mean_capped_normalized_rmse\",\n        \"data_role\": \"final_evaluation_plan\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"mean_absolute_capped_normalized_bias\",\n        \"data_role\": \"final_evaluation_plan\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"failed_episode_fraction\",\n        \"data_role\": \"final_evaluation_plan\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"control_success_fraction\",\n        \"data_role\": \"final_evaluation_plan\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"upstream\": [\n    {\n      \"repository\": \"h