,\n      1091,\n      1093,\n      1097,\n      1103,\n      1109,\n      1117,\n      1123,\n      1129,\n      1151,\n      1153,\n      1163,\n      1009,\n      1013,\n      1019,\n      1021,\n      1031,\n      1033,\n      1039,\n      1049,\n      1051,\n      1061,\n      1063,\n      1069,\n      1087,\n      1091,\n      1093,\n      1097,\n      1103,\n      1109,\n      1117,\n      1123,\n      1129,\n      1151,\n      1153,\n      1163,\n      1009,\n      1013,\n      1019,\n      1021,\n      1031,\n      1033,\n      1039,\n      1049,\n      1051,\n      1061,\n      1063,\n      1069,\n      1087,\n      1091,\n      1093,\n      1097,\n      1103,\n      1109,\n      1117,\n      1123,\n      1129,\n      1151,\n      1153,\n      1163,\n      1009\n    ],\n    \"search_smoke_reset_sequence\": [\n      101,\n      101,\n      101,\n      101,\n      101\n    ],\n    \"final_smoke_reset_sequence\": [\n      1009,\n      1009,\n      1009,\n      1009,\n      1009\n    ],\n    \"baselines\": [\n      \"difference_in_means\",\n      \"own_treatment_ols\",\n      \"one_hop_ols\",\n      \"copy_observed\",\n      \"constant_prediction\"\n    ],\n    \"promotion_rule\": \"Harness only: at most three complete production search evaluations, one per idea attempt. Eligibility requires search correct=true, not baseline improvement or significance. Rank eligible candidates by combined_score descending; exact ties prefer earliest completed evaluation, then lexicographic frozen source SHA-256. Freeze before sealed final. Scientific validity, search eligibility and final claim assessment are separate. Ordered case-major production primary episodes: search SBM/BA/WS x M0..M5 x eight seeds, then constant and permutation each x eight seeds (160); final SBM/BA/WS/Stanford3 x M0..M5 x 24 seeds, then constant/permutation each x 24 (624). Exactly one trailing replay of the first selected seed is always performed after each declared primary sequence; its reset is included in every complete ordered global reset array, including smoke and across all connections. Smoke primary sequence is M0,M2,constant,permutation on first seed, then same sole replay (five episodes total). RPC table per episode: reset 1 + ingest at most 8 + fit 1 + predict 1 =11; first/last ingest performs setup/commit, no hidden transfer calls. Search 161*11=1771; final 625*11=6875; smoke 5*11=55. All controls and replay retain fixed finite failure slots. Missing or unsuccessful controls make qualification infeasible. No candidate state flags or internal counters are scientific evidence.\",\n    \"search_proxies\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"small_synthetic_search\",\n        \"preserves\": \"Six DGPs, three synthetic graph families, paired seed experiments, endpoint estimand, actual baselines and matched constant/permutation/reset behavior, finite penalties and fixed hierarchy.\",\n        \"omits\": \"Larger 4096-node fresh synthetic graphs, full 11586-node Stanford3, 24 sealed seeds, and final external-validity assessment. Search has 1024 nodes and eight seeds; search feedback never contains final values.\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"feedback\": {\n    \"search_visible\": [\n      \"Public scientific question, allowed starting literature and access restrictions; documented plane-independent handle protocol, permitted input semantics and finite resource ceilings; synthetic search definitions and evaluator-computed search scalar metrics/correctness plus permitted search diagnostics.\",\n      \"Candidate receives only its current episode's topology, covariates, realized assignment and observed experimental outcomes, permitted prediction assignments and public fitting configuration. Search-visible artifacts must not embed concrete final seeds, final manifests, final-seed constants, final assets or seed-to-workload mappings.\",\n      \"At most three idea cycles and one production candidate evaluation per attempt, three total. Each evaluation contains the entire declared search plan. Use deterministic eligibility, combined_score ranking and tie policy above; freeze the selected eligible source/configuration before final access. Wiring smoke cannot become extra scored candidate selection.\"\n    ],\n    \"final_sealed\": [\n      \"Final concrete seeds and split manifests, final synthetic graph instances and observations, selected public-graph resource copy and all unobserved potential outcomes/true GATE values remain evaluator-owned until freeze; reveal only the permitted current-episode observations through RPC.\",\n      \"Final baseline outputs, per-episode errors, scores, correctness, control judgments, uncertainty calculations, endpoint targets and claim assessment never enter candidate requests or search feedback. Final evidence is released only for post-freeze assessment/reporting, not candidate tuning or selection.\",\n      \"Privileged evaluator source/manifests/design/contract may record the final seed transcript; they are not candidate-visible starter material. Cross-role resource enforcement and allocation evidence are harness-owned; handle has no memory, telemetry or peer-resource accessor.\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"publication\": {\n    \"search_is_proxy\": true,\n    \"requires_final_evaluation\": true,\n    \"required_evidence\": [\n      \"A completed paper PDF and LaTeX source using the latest official template of one chosen allowed conference, with verified current main-text page limit and required checklist. Include abstract, introduction, real consulted related work, method, experimental design, results, discussion, limitations and references. Publication quality/novelty review is separate from search eligibility and final operational correct.\",\n      \"Independent derivation of the finite-population endpoint estimand, linear correctly specified plug-in behavior and the role of unsupported extrapolation or omitted exposure terms. State testable hypotheses and interference/graph/design scope before scoring; distinguish model-dependent extrapolation from nonparametric identification and conditional public-topology results from general platform claims.\",\n      \"Actual reproducible completed-run records for all scientific cases, baselines, controls and the sole replay, including failures, abandoned candidates and budget-limited omissions. Provide paired seed-block uncertainty for bias/RMSE and baseline differences, per-family/mechanism tables, exposure-support/conditioning diagnostics, uncapped tails and clipping frequency. With only eight search and 24 final seeds per case, report Monte Carlo limitations and avoid node-independent standard errors. Do not fabricate numerical results, confidence intervals, launches, checkpoints or completed production validation.\",\n      \"Evaluator-owned raw archive and normalized graph/example digests, source/row provenance, normalization rules fixed before splitting/features, randomization/generator seeds and nonoverlapping search/final split manifests. Show content-level cross-plane intersection checks, including different-ID duplicates and relabeling provenance. Record the Stanford3 supplied revision verification and applicable license/attribution; shared immutable code is not a held-out data violation.\",\n      \"A frozen candidate/source/dependency digest and selection record showing at most three production search evaluations, each from its declared complete plan, eligibility independent of baseline superiority, combined_score ranking and deterministic tie handling before final access. Record that final results were not used for tuning or additional candidate evaluations.\",\n      \"Scaffold and validation must provide standard contract provenance, exact serialized maximum-size request/response measurements including JSON/base64/envelope/framing, strict sub-64-MiB checks, candidate-owned in-memory chunk handling and a complete RPC budget derivation. Validate the exact production and smoke reset arrays against every case-seed episode globally across connections. Retain actual transport-count and reset evidence; no shared-path RPC or private-target leakage is permissible.\",\n      \"Offline empty-HOME dependency validation and same-path 120-second smoke evidence for both planes, followed separately by actual full-production completion/failure evidence under enforced wall, aggregate all-thread CPU, memory and broker limits. Identify candidate objective evaluations, ridge-grid/solver iterations and reported internal counts as advisory unless independently counted by a trusted service; never present them as enforced internal compute caps. Smoke cannot attest full workload completion. No cross-role telemetry access is assumed.\",\n      \"Evaluator-owned negative-control evidence must show matched inputs/budgets, actual candidate fit and prediction execution, expected constant/zero contrast behavior, effective nonidentity permutation/equivariance and exactly one trailing reset replay. Null copy/constant baselines cannot stand in for the claimed method. Missing or failed controls and cases retain their predeclared finite worst-case contributions and original weights; a vacuous permutation yields no causal conclusion.\",\n      \"Complete reproducibility instructions with environment versions, offline installation approach, data acquisition/version/license, seeds, commands and measured eventual runtimes, plus a trace from every reported table/figure to actual run outputs and its generating code. Later scaffold additions beyond standard files require concrete task-relative paths and actual SHA-256 provenance with contract resynchronization. The week-long project limit includes implementation, no more than 2700 seconds of production search, 7200 seconds of final evaluation, analysis and writing; no unbudgeted extra candidate campaign is assumed.\",\n      \"Respect the canonical prohibition on the unnamed prior paper and all mirrors, summaries, code, discussion or follow-on pages about it. Do not infer its identity or search for its title/authors/results. Use only allowed starting references actually consulted and unrelated permitted material. Restrict asset acquisition to the supplied data URL; if prohibited content is accidentally encountered, stop immediately and record where, what and how much was seen in reproducibility notes. Missing referenced deliverable/resources/data sidecars are not supplied inputs; the requirements embedded in task.md are authoritative, and no sidecar contents or hidden harness behavior are presumed.\",\n      \"Contract reset arrays enumerate the entire ordered invocation, including the sole trailing deterministic replay: 161 search production resets, 625 final production resets and five resets in each smoke profile. Validate all four arrays against the executable case-major episode plans globally across connections; reconnections and process restarts never restart the transcript.\",\n      \"This scaffold is an operational test, not an automated conference review or proof of model internals. Full research PDF and LaTeX, latest official conference template/checklist, independent derivations, actually consulted permitted citations, paired seed-block uncertainty, uncapped tails and every figure/table reproduction remain required paper-stage work. No positive comparative threshold is authorized.\",\n      \"Low-level graph-cluster definition is deterministic balanced BFS over actual topology, not an optimized published design. M4 is length-two walk exposure including backtracking, not a unique-distance-two mean. Relabel-invariant multiset fingerprints conservatively reject possible graph overlap and raw row hashes exclude IDs. Frozen manifests document these scope limitations.\",\n      \"Linux native smoke requires functioning Landlock ABI 3 and libseccomp.so.2; CPython 3.11/3.12 wheels are pinned. No Python/CUDA/driver entries are pip packages. Empty-HOME local-data execution and bounded native file/network isolation are validated; actual production broker/container closure remains harness-owned.\"\n    ]\n  }\n}\n[\n  \"campaign_results_dir\",\n  \"count\",\n  \"generated_at\",\n  \"queries\",\n  \"reference_query_plan\",\n  \"references\",\n  \"results_dir\"\n]\n@Article{Chin2018RegressionAF,\n@Article{Han2023ModelbasedRA,\n@Article{Srivastava1989SteinEU,\n@Article{Singh1991JAMESSTEINRE,\n@Article{Chen2015OnDO,\n@Article{Hofheinz2014HeteroscedasticRR,\n@Article{Blaker2000MinimaxEI,\n@Inproceedings{Chaturvedi1990STEINRE,\n@Article{Arashi2014ShrinkageRE,\n@Article{Roozbeh2023GeneralizedSV,\n@Article{Asl2020PenalizedAR,\n@Article{Ueki2016SmooththresholdMG,\n@Article{Herbreteau2022TowardsAU,\n@Article{Asl2019RidgetypeSE,\n@Article{Bischoff1991NormalDA,\n@Article{Zhang2021SketchedQA,\n@Article{Yuasa2020RidgetypeLS,\n@Inproceedings{Reangsephet2020PostSE,\n@Article{Zhang2023AFO,\n@Inproceedings{Zhang2022FunctionalLR,\n@Article{Liu2016PositiveruleSA,\n@Article{Lin2023GlobalDD,\n@Article{Yang2017OnEA,\n@Inproceedings{Sardy2011SmoothJM,\n@Inproceedings{Yuasa2019RidgetypeLS,\n---\nname: generate-concept-figure\ndescription: Generate one reader-facing conceptual overview figure for paper generation as an editable draw.io diagram via the pinned Autoillustrate npm release, with a deterministic layout and an optional image-model restyle.\n---\n\n# Who runs this (important)\nDuring **paper generation the orchestrator owns this pipeline**: `src/scripts/paper.sh` and `paper_edit.sh` run the installed `autoillustrate` CLI synchronously as a post-draft step (`run_concept_figure_step`), derive every argument from `paper_strategy.json`, forward the selected outer agent, and promote the result to `./figures/<figure_id>.png`. The phase agents always run in a dedicated one-shot Docker container, even when the outer paper workflow is native; this limits them to the paper directory, selected-agent auth, and selected provider credentials. The paper-writing agent must **not** invoke this pipeline itself. The rest of this document describes the same CLI for standalone/manual use.\n\n# What the skill is about\nGenerate one reader-facing conceptual overview figure for the paper when a high-level glance-value visual will clarify the method, comparison story, or evidence structure. The figure is produced by the Autoillustrate pipeline (the `autoillustrate` npm release pinned in the agent image): each panel is a collision-checked, deterministically laid-out draw.io diagram, the panels are composed into a single editable `.drawio` file, and the composite is optionally restyled into a camera-ready PNG. The deliverable is a real `.drawio` source plus its export — only the final restyle pass touches a generative model.\n\n# When to use the skill\n- Final paper generation.\n- The paper needs an early conceptual figure that is easier to scan than a dense quantitative plot.\n- The grounded artifacts support a clean overview figure without inventing unsupported mechanisms or claims.\n- `paper_strategy.json` requests a required overview-style `diagram` figure or the paper prompt calls for an overview figure on page 1 or 2.\n- The figure is a methods/architecture/training-loop schematic with 1–3 structurally distinct panels. (For pure quantitative plots use matplotlib/seaborn instead.)\n\n# Prerequisites\nThe pipeline shells out to several tools. Confirm them before claiming a hard failure:\n- **`drawio` desktop CLI** on `PATH` (headless export). Without it Phases 2/4 cannot export.\n- **`autoillustrate` and `headless`** on `PATH`, plus the selected agent CLI (`claude`, `codex`, `cursor`, `gemini`, `opencode`, or `pi`).\n- For environment-authenticated OpenCode phase agents, set `PAPER_CONCEPT_FIGURE_AGENT_PROVIDER` to exactly one of `openai`, `gemini`, or `anthropic`; only that provider credential is forwarded.\n- **`OPENAI_API_KEY`** — the default VLM backend (`gpt-5.5`) for the Phase 3 per-panel inspection and the Phase 6 verification, and the image model (`gpt-image-2`) for the Phase 5 restyle. Without it those VLM calls and the restyle cannot run; you can still ship the deterministic Phase 4 export with `--skip-enhance`.\n- **`GEMINI_API_KEY`** — optional fallback. When OpenAI is unavailable, the paper orchestrator selects `nanobanana-pro`, `gemini-3.1-pro`, and `gemini-single` for enhancement and audits.\n- **A Python venv** with the toolkit deps. The container image bakes one and exposes its interpreter as `$VENV_PY`.\n\nBefore deciding a key is missing, check the active environment directly. OpenAI is the default; Gemini is the automatic fallback:\n```bash\npython - <<'PY'\nimport os\nfor k in (\"OPENAI_API_KEY\", \"GEMINI_API_KEY\"):\n    print(f\"{k}: {'available' if os.getenv(k) else 'missing'}\")\nPY\n```\nDo not claim a key is unavailable when the rendered paper prompt says it is expected to be available unless your direct check still shows it missing. Without an enhancement key, `--skip-enhance` still ships the deterministic Phase 4 export.\n\n# What to do\n1. Infer the central mechanism, comparison, or evidence story from grounded artifacts only. Decide whether one cohesive panel suffices or the content naturally splits into 2–3 structurally independent panels (e.g. *architecture · update rule · training loop*). Prefer one overview figure, not a full illustration suite.\n\n2. Confirm the installed CLI and selected agent are available:\n```bash\ncommand -v autoillustrate\nautoillustrate doctor --agent \"${AGENT:-claude}\"\n```\n\n3. In the project container, use the baked `$VENV_PY`. Native installations may let Autoillustrate create its cached venv or set `VENV_PY` explicitly.\n\n4. Run the pipeline against the manuscript. Resolve the strategy's exact figure id, pass `--output ./figures/<figure_id>.png`, forward the selected `--agent`, and provide a concise grounded prompt. Add `--skip-enhance` when no enhancement backend is available.\n\n**This pipeline can take ~1h** (it dispatches several selected-agent jobs and may run a VLM restyle). Run it **synchronously and block on it** — the caller must own the pipeline's full lifetime. Do **not** launch it as a background task that outlives the caller's turn (`run_in_background: true`, a trailing `&`, or a fire-and-forget agent step): when that turn ends the pipeline is orphaned and reaped mid-run, leaving the figure unrendered. In `paper.sh` and `paper_edit.sh` this is exactly what `run_concept_figure_step` does — a single synchronous invocation in the agent container, wrapped with `timeout` or Homebrew's `gtimeout` so a genuine hang is bounded. Native systems without either command skip this non-gating render step instead of launching an unbounded process. The pipeline writes `./figures/<figure_id>.png` (and `<figure_id>.prompts.json`) only on success; confirm those files exist before treating the figure as done.\n```bash\nautoillustrate ./paper.tex \\\n  --output ./figures/<figure_id>.png \\\n  --agent \"${AGENT:-claude}\" \\\n  --prompt \"Methods diagram that will be the main figure of this scientific research paper. <one or two sentences grounding the panels in the actual method>\"\n```\nThe orchestrator creates `runs/<YYYY-MM-DD-HHMMSS>/` in the working directory and writes the deliverables to `runs/<ts>/figures/`:\n- `full_figure.drawio` — editable draw.io source\n- `full_figure.png` — deterministic export (no model involved; always safe)\n- `full_figure_enhanced.png` — publication-grade restyle (only when Phase 5 ran)\n- `figure.json` — the validated 1–3 panel plan that drove the figure\n\nWith `--output` set, the pipeline also copies the best available figure (the enhanced export when Phase 5 ran, otherwise the deterministic export) to `./figures/<figure_id>.png` and drops the plan beside it as `./figures/<figure_id>.prompts.json`. The pipeline does not emit a PDF; the editable `full_figure.drawio` stays in the run workdir.\n\n5. Keep the visual style scientific and simple: clean diagrammatic composition, exact labels, no decorative clip-art, no unsupported architecture details, datasets, or numeric claims. When the paper contains multiple figures, keep colors logically consistent — reuse the same color for the same method/baseline/condition across figures.\n\n6. Confirm the promoted deliverable. With `--output` (step 4) the pipeline already wrote `./figures/<figure_id>.png` and `./figures/<figure_id>.prompts.json` — verify both exist. If you ran without `--output`, promote manually from the run workdir (enhanced export preferred, deterministic export as fallback):\n```bash\nRUN_FIGS=\"$(ls -td runs/*/figures | head -1)\"\nSRC_PNG=\"$RUN_FIGS/full_figure_enhanced.png\"; [[ -f \"$SRC_PNG\" ]] || SRC_PNG=\"$RUN_FIGS/full_figure.png\"\ncp \"$SRC_PNG\" \"./figures/<figure_id>.png\"\ncp \"$RUN_FIGS/figure.json\" \"./figures/<figure_id>.prompts.json\"   # the prompt/plan log\n```\nThe editable `full_figure.drawio` stays in the run workdir so the figure can be re-edited later. The pipeline produces no PDF; the manifest does not require one for this figure.\n\n7. When the strategy or prompt asks for a required overview/`diagram` figure, do not silently replace this workflow with a hand-drawn or purely matplotlib/TikZ schematic. Use this skill first unless it is impossible.\n\n8. If a prerequisite is missing (for example, no `drawio` CLI) or the pipeline fails, log an explicit skip/failure reason in both `./memory.md` and `./global_memory/memory.md` before falling back to another figure implementation. Apply the same fallback logging rule if the generated figure is too poor to use.\n\n9. If you fall back to a non-drawio overview figure, record that fallback reason in the matching `figure_manifest.json` note so the run leaves a clear breadcrumb.\n\n10. If the final figure is used in `paper.tex`, add a matching `figure_manifest.json` entry that records `generator: generate-concept-figure`, `prompt_log_path` (the copied `./figures/<figure_id>.prompts.json`), and any `fallback_reason`. If the figure is not used, do not force it into the manuscript.\n\n# Outputs\n- `./figures/<figure_id>.png` (promoted from `full_figure_enhanced.png`, or `full_figure.png` when enhancement was skipped)\n- `./figures/<figure_id>.prompts.json` (the run's `figure.json` plan, used as `prompt_log_path`)\n- Editable source preserved at `runs/<ts>/figures/full_figure.drawio`\n- Legacy explicit-path form remains valid: `./figures/concept_figure.png` and `./figures/concept_figure.prompts.json`\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Append validated local/global memory entries for idea workflows.\n\nTwo modes:\n\n* default (event append) — appends one memory event to ``memory.md`` (local +\n  global) plus one JSONL record to ``memory.jsonl``. Existing behavior.\n* ``--write-conclusions`` — atomically replaces ``conclusions.md`` with a\n  validated single-paragraph distilled summary and appends a record to\n  ``conclusions_history.jsonl``. Validation rejects empty input,\n  multi-paragraph input, or input over 300 words.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport fcntl\nimport json\nimport os\nimport stat\nimport sys\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Any\n\nCONCLUSIONS_WORD_LIMIT = 300\nGATE_TRIGGER_VALUES = (\"a\", \"b\", \"c\", \"d\")\n\nLOCAL_MEMORY_HEADERS = \"\"\"# Memory Log\n\n## Context\n## Idea Discoveries\n## Program Evaluations\n## Failures / Regressions\n## Next Hypotheses\n\"\"\"\n\nGLOBAL_MEMORY_HEADER = \"# Global Memory Log\\n\\n\"\n\n\ndef utc_now() -> str:\n    \"\"\"Return the current UTC timestamp string.\"\"\"\n    return datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat()\n\n\ndef _load_event(*, event_json: str | None, event_file: Path | None) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Load event.\"\"\"\n    if event_json:\n        parsed = json.loads(event_json)\n    elif event_file is not None:\n        parsed = json.loads(event_file.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n    else:\n        raw = input().strip()\n        if not raw:\n            raise ValueError(\"missing event payload\")\n        parsed = json.loads(raw)\n    if not isinstance(parsed, dict):\n        raise ValueError(\"event payload must be a JSON object\")\n    return parsed\n\n\ndef _ensure_required_fields(event: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Ensure required fields.\"\"\"\n    normalized = dict(event)\n    if not isinstance(normalized.get(\"timestamp\"), str) or not normalized[\"timestamp\"].strip():\n        normalized[\"timestamp\"] = utc_now()\n\n    required_string_fields = (\"step\", \"scope\", \"summary\", \"evidence\", \"next_action\")\n    for key in required_string_fields:\n        value = normalized.get(key)\n        if not isinstance(value, str) or not value.strip():\n            raise ValueError(f\"missing required string field: {key}\")\n        normalized[key] = value.strip()\n\n    for key in (\"idea_id\", \"attempt_id\", \"program_id\"):\n        value = normalized.get(key)\n        if value is None:\n            continue\n        if not isinstance(value, str):\n            normalized[key] = str(value)\n        normalized[key] = normalized[key].strip() or None\n\n    metrics = normalized.get(\"metrics\")\n    if metrics is not None and not isinstance(metrics, dict):\n        raise ValueError(\"metrics must be an object when present\")\n    rubrics = normalized.get(\"rubrics\")\n    if rubrics is not None and not isinstance(rubrics, list):\n        raise ValueError(\"rubrics must be an array when present\")\n    tags = normalized.get(\"tags\")\n    if tags is not None:\n        if not isinstance(tags, list):\n            raise ValueError(\"tags must be an array when present\")\n        normalized[\"tags\"] = [str(item).strip() for item in tags if str(item).strip()]\n    return normalized\n\n\ndef _markdown_entry(event: dict[str, Any]) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Handle markdown entry logic for this module.\"\"\"\n    lines = [\n        f\"### {event['timestamp']} | step={event['step']} | scope={event['scope']}\",\n        f\"- summary: {event['summary']}\",\n        f\"- evidence: {event['evidence']}\",\n        f\"- next_action: {event['next_action']}\",\n    ]\n\n    for key in (\"idea_id\", \"attempt_id\", \"program_id\"):\n        value = event.get(key)\n        if isinstance(value, str) and value.strip():\n            lines.append(f\"- {key}: {value.strip()}\")\n\n    metrics = event.get(\"metrics\")\n    if isinstance(metrics, dict) and metrics:\n        lines.append(f\"- metrics: {json.dumps(metrics, sort_keys=True)}\")\n    rubrics = event.get(\"rubrics\")\n    if isinstance(rubrics, list) and rubrics:\n        lines.append(f\"- rubrics: {json.dumps(rubrics, sort_keys=True)}\")\n    tags = event.get(\"tags\")\n    if isinstance(tags, list) and tags:\n        lines.append(f\"- tags: {', '.join(str(item) for item in tags)}\")\n\n    return \"\\n\".join(lines) + \"\\n\\n\"\n\n\ndef _append_text(path: Path, text: str, *, header: str) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Safely initialize and append text to a regular file.\"\"\"\n    fd = _open_regular_for_append(path)\n    try:\n        fcntl.flock(fd, fcntl.LOCK_EX)\n        size = os.fstat(fd).st_size\n        if not size:\n            _write_all(fd, header.encode(\"utf-8\"))\n        elif os.pread(fd, 1, size - 1) != b\"\\n\":\n            _write_all(fd, b\"\\n\")\n        _write_all(fd, text.encode(\"utf-8\"))\n    finally:\n        try:\n            fcntl.flock(fd, fcntl.LOCK_UN)\n        finally:\n            os.close(fd)\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"sed -n '108,260p' results/ideas/03_endpoint_contrast_sure_for_exposure_regression/program_1/src/program.py; jq '{keys:keys,graph_keys:(.graphs|type),other:([to_entries[]|select((.value|type)\"'!=\"array\" and (.value|type)!=\"object\")])}'\"' task/resources/final/manifest.json; jq 'keys' references_provenance.json; rg '\"'^@'\"' references.bib; rg -n 'mechanism|true_gate|noise|bernoulli|SBM|Stanford|normal|probability|seed|manifest' task/evaluate.py | head -90; sed -n '1,80p' .codex/skills/generate-concept-figure/SKILL.md; ls -la ../final_evaluation\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"sed -n '108,260p' results/ideas/03_endpoint_contrast_sure_for_exposure_regression/program_1/src/program.py; jq '{keys:keys,graph_keys:(.graphs|type),other:([to_entries[]|select((.value|type)\"'!=\"array\" and (.value|type)!=\"object\")])}'\"' task/resources/final/manifest.json; jq 'keys' references_provenance.json; rg '\"'^@'\"' references.bib; rg -n 'mechanism|true_gate|noise|bernoulli|SBM|Stanford|normal|probability|seed|manifest' task/evaluate.py | head -90; sed -n '1,80p' .codex/skills/generate-concept-figure/SKILL.md; ls -la ../final_evaluation\"","aggregated_output":"            and np.all(np.isfinite(feature_scale))\n            and np.all(np.isfinite(standardized_design))\n            and np.all(np.isfinite(endpoint_contrast))\n            and np.all(np.isfinite(centered_outcome))):\n        return _fit_incumbent(assignment, outcome)\n    try:\n        left_vectors, singular_values, right_vectors = np.linalg.svd(\n            standardized_design, full_matrices=False)\n    except np.linalg.LinAlgError:\n        return _fit_incumbent(assignment, outcome)\n    if not (np.all(np.isfinite(singular_values))\n            and np.all(np.isfinite(left_vectors))\n            and np.all(np.isfinite(right_vectors))):\n        return _fit_incumbent(assignment, outcome)\n    retained = singular_values > max(standardized_design.shape) * np.finfo(np.float64).eps * singular_values[0]\n    contrast_coordinates = right_vectors[retained] @ endpoint_contrast\n    estimability_error = np.linalg.norm(endpoint_contrast - right_vectors[retained].T @ contrast_coordinates)\n    if not np.isfinite(estimability_error):\n        return _fit_incumbent(assignment, outcome)\n    if estimability_error > 1e-8 * max(1.0, np.linalg.norm(endpoint_contrast)):\n        return _fit_incumbent(assignment, outcome)\n    if outcome.size - int(np.count_nonzero(retained)) - 1 <= 0:\n        return _fit_incumbent(assignment, outcome)\n    reference_weights = left_vectors[:, retained] @ (contrast_coordinates / singular_values[retained])\n    projected_outcome = left_vectors[:, retained].T @ centered_outcome\n    residual = centered_outcome - left_vectors[:, retained] @ projected_outcome\n    noise_variance = float(residual @ residual) / (outcome.size - int(np.count_nonzero(retained)) - 1)\n    reference_effect = float(reference_weights @ centered_outcome)\n    if not (np.all(np.isfinite(reference_weights))\n            and np.isfinite(noise_variance) and np.isfinite(reference_effect)):\n        return _fit_incumbent(assignment, outcome)\n    penalties = outcome.size * np.array([0.0, 1e-6, 1e-4, 1e-2, 1.0])\n    risk_scores = []\n    with np.errstate(over='ignore', invalid='ignore', divide='ignore'):\n        for penalty in penalties:\n            contrast_weights = left_vectors[:, retained] @ (singular_values[retained] * contrast_coordinates / (singular_values[retained] ** 2 + penalty))\n            risk_score = float((contrast_weights @ centered_outcome - reference_effect) ** 2 + 2.0 * noise_variance * (contrast_weights @ reference_weights) - noise_variance * (reference_weights @ reference_weights))\n            risk_scores.append(risk_score if np.isfinite(risk_score) else np.inf)\n    if not np.any(np.isfinite(risk_scores)):\n        return _fit_incumbent(assignment, outcome)\n    selected_index = int(np.argmin(risk_scores))\n    penalty = penalties[selected_index]\n    coefficients = right_vectors[retained].T @ (\n        singular_values[retained] * projected_outcome\n        / (singular_values[retained] ** 2 + penalty))\n    if not np.all(np.isfinite(coefficients)):\n        return _fit_incumbent(assignment, outcome)\n    return {'kind': 'endpoint_sure', 'coefficients': coefficients,\n            'feature_mean': feature_mean, 'feature_scale': feature_scale,\n            'outcome_mean': outcome_mean}\n\n\ndef _predict_endpoint_sure(assignment, model):\n    if model['kind'] == 'incumbent':\n        return _features(assignment) @ model['coefficients']\n    design = _reference_features(assignment)\n    standardized_design = (design[:, 1:] - model['feature_mean']) / model['feature_scale']\n    return model['outcome_mean'] + standardized_design @ model['coefficients']\n\n\ndef handle(request):\n    operation = request['op']\n    if operation == 'reset':\n        _state.clear()\n        _state['seed'] = request['seed']\n        _state['chunks'] = []\n        return {'ok': True}\n    if operation == 'ingest':\n        metadata = tuple(request[name] for name in ('n', 'p', 'm', 'total'))\n        count, width, edge_count, total = metadata\n        if not (0 < count <= 12000 and 0 < width <= 8 and 0 <= edge_count <= 600000\n                and 0 < total <= 8 and request['index'] == len(_state['chunks'])):\n            raise ValueError('invalid ingestion')\n        if 'metadata' in _state and _state['metadata'] != metadata:\n            raise ValueError('metadata changed')\n        _state['metadata'] = metadata\n        chunk = base64.b64decode(request['data'], validate=True)\n        if len(chunk) > 4 * 1024 * 1024:\n            raise ValueError('chunk too large')\n        _state['chunks'].append(chunk)\n        if len(_state['chunks']) == total:\n            packed = b''.join(_state.pop('chunks'))\n            expected = 8 * edge_count + 8 * count * width + 9 * count\n            if len(packed) != expected or expected > 32 * 1024 * 1024:\n                raise ValueError('invalid data length')\n            _state['n'] = count\n            _state['edges'] = np.frombuffer(packed, '<i4', 2 * edge_count).reshape(-1, 2)\n            _state['x'] = np.frombuffer(packed, '<f8', count * width, 8 * edge_count).reshape(count, width)\n            _state['z'] = np.frombuffer(packed, 'u1', count, 8 * edge_count + 8 * count * width).astype(float)\n            _state['y'] = np.frombuffer(packed, '<f8', count, 8 * edge_count + 8 * count * width + count)\n        return {'ok': True}\n    if operation == 'fit':\n        _state['constant_outcome'] = bool(np.all(_state['y'] == _state['y'][0]))\n        if _state['constant_outcome']:\n            _state['model'] = None\n        else:\n            _state['model'] = _fit_endpoint_sure(_state['z'], _state['y'])\n        return {'ok': True}\n    if operation == 'predict':\n        if _state['constant_outcome']:\n            predictions = np.full((3, _state['n']), float(_state['y'][0]), dtype=np.float64)\n        else:\n            predictions = np.stack([_predict_endpoint_sure(assignment, _state['model']) for assignment in (_state['z'], np.ones(_state['n']), np.zeros(_state['n']))])\n        return {'encoding': 'base64', 'dtype': '<f8', 'shape': [3, _state['n']],\n                'data': base64.b64encode(predictions.astype('<f8').tobytes()).decode('ascii')}\n    raise ValueError('unsupported operation')\n{\n  \"keys\": [\n    \"aggregation\",\n    \"attribution\",\n    \"benchmark_sha256\",\n    \"controls\",\n    \"families\",\n    \"generator\",\n    \"graph_fingerprints\",\n    \"mechanisms\",\n    \"normalization\",\n    \"plan\",\n    \"plane\",\n    \"preflight\",\n    \"records\",\n    \"rows\",\n    \"schema_version\",\n    \"seeds\",\n    \"split_audit\",\n    \"time_plan\"\n  ],\n  \"graph_keys\": \"null\",\n  \"other\": [\n    {\n      \"key\": \"schema_version\",\n      \"value\": 1\n    },\n    {\n      \"key\": \"plane\",\n      \"value\": \"final\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"key\": \"benchmark_sha256\",\n      \"value\": \"ba5ae5cd05e4b310a1c0dd40bf15568fd489c35704cb5812642de117fe878832\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"key\": \"normalization\",\n      \"value\": \"Undirected sorted int32 unique pairs, remove self-loops, preserve declared n/isolates; float64 little endian and signed zero normalized. IDs excluded. Relabel-invariant conservative structural-context multiset graph fingerprint; rows hash raw x,z,y plus sorted neighbor-degree context. Hash collisions are conservative rejection, not accepted disjointness. No text examples.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"key\": \"generator\",\n      \"value\": \"NetworkX 3.3; four-block SBM p_in=.04 p_out=.002; BA m=5; WS k=10 rewire=.15. RNG PCG64 with seed +100003*(family ordinal+1). Independent graph/observation statistical seeds across planes.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"key\": \"mechanisms\",\n      \"value\": \"tau=1; x coefficient .5; unit fixed Gaussian noise sd1. M0 no spill; M1 .25*neighbor mean; M2 2*neighbor mean; M3 2*I(mean>=.75)+z*mean; M4 2*mean(neighbor means), length-two random walks with backtracking; M5 M2 with 32 deterministic balanced graph-BFS clusters: start smallest unassigned node, traverse sorted CSR neighbors, assign up to ceil(n/32), restart at smallest unassigned when frontier empties, discard frontier between clusters. Independent cluster p=.5. Isolate neighbor means=0. Not claimed optimal clustering.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"key\": \"controls\",\n      \"value\": \"constant y=3.25 on SBM M2, nonidentity reversal of all SBM M2 rows and edges, reset replay first scientific episode; within-plane reuse is intentional. Tolerances atol=rtol=1e-6.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"key\": \"rows\",\n      \"value\": 3095842\n    },\n    {\n      \"key\": \"graph_fingerprints\",\n      \"value\": 73\n    },\n    {\n      \"key\": \"attribution\",\n      \"value\": \"Stanford3: Rossi & Ahmed (AAAI 2015), Traud, Mucha & Porter (Physica A 2012). Network Repository CC BY-SA as verified in canonical task; version not specified. Retain attribution and share-alike obligations. Archive checksum and 11586/568309 dimensions verified; no SNAP acquisition or restricted literature access.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n[\n  \"campaign_results_dir\",\n  \"count\",\n  \"generated_at\",\n  \"queries\",\n  \"reference_query_plan\",\n  \"references\",\n  \"results_dir\"\n]\n@Article{Chin2018RegressionAF,\n@Article{Han2023ModelbasedRA,\n@Article{Srivastava1989SteinEU,\n@Article{Singh1991JAMESSTEINRE,\n@Article{Chen2015OnDO,\n@Article{Hofheinz2014HeteroscedasticRR,\n@Article{Blaker2000MinimaxEI,\n@Inproceedings{Chaturvedi1990STEINRE,\n@Article{Arashi2014ShrinkageRE,\n@Article{Roozbeh2023GeneralizedSV,\n@Article{Asl2020PenalizedAR,\n@Article{Ueki2016SmooththresholdMG,\n@Article{Herbreteau2022TowardsAU,\n@Article{Asl2019RidgetypeSE,\n@Article{Bischoff1991NormalDA,\n@Article{Zhang2021SketchedQA,\n@Article{Yuasa2020RidgetypeLS,\n@Inproceedings{Reangsephet2020PostSE,\n@Article{Zhang2023AFO,\n@Inproceedings{Zhang2022FunctionalLR,\n@Article{Liu2016PositiveruleSA,\n@Article{Lin2023GlobalDD,\n@Article{Yang2017OnEA,\n@Inproceedings{Sardy2011SmoothJM,\n@Inproceedings{Yuasa2019RidgetypeLS,\n46:METRICS = ('combined_score', 'mean_capped_normalized_rmse', 'mean_absolute_capped_normalized_bias',\n654:            require_reset_ack(rpc({'op': 'reset', 'seed': episode['seed']}, timeout=timeout))\n676:def normalize_edges(edges):\n686:def potential_outcome(assignment, covariates, noise, edges, mechanism):\n692:             2 * (exposure >= .75) + assignment * exposure, 2 * two_hop, 2 * exposure][mechanism]\n693:    return .5 * covariates[:, 0] + assignment + spill + noise\n731:    manifest_bytes = (root / 'manifest.json').read_bytes()\n732:    if hashlib.sha256(manifest_bytes).hexdigest() != MANIFEST_SHA256:\n733:        raise ValueError('manifest integrity failure')\n734:    manifest = json.loads(manifest_bytes)\n736:    if hashlib.sha256(archive_path.read_bytes()).hexdigest() != manifest['benchmark_sha256']:\n738:    audit = manifest['split_audit']\n739:    if (audit['normalized_graph_intersections'] != 0 or audit['normalized_raw_example_intersections'] != 0\n740:            or not audit['source_seed_sets_disjoint'] or not audit['checked_before_fitting']):\n743:        archive = root / 'Stanford3.zip'\n751:            public_edges = normalize_edges([[int(value) - 1 for value in line.split()[:2]] for line in lines[1:]])\n753:    if PLANE == 'final' and not np.array_equal(data['Stanford3_edges'], public_edges):\n754:        raise ValueError('public normalization failure')\n755:    return manifest, data\n758:def episode_plan(manifest, smoke):\n759:    seeds = manifest['seeds'][:1] if smoke else manifest['seeds']\n760:    families = [manifest['families'][-1] if PLANE == 'final' else 'SBM'] if smoke else manifest['families']\n761:    mechanisms = [0, 2] if smoke else list(range(6))\n762:    episodes = [{'kind': 'scientific', 'family': family, 'mechanism': mechanism, 'seed': seed}\n763:                for family in families for mechanism in mechanisms for seed in seeds]\n764:    control_family = families[0] if smoke else 'SBM'\n766:        episodes.extend({'kind': kind, 'family': control_family, 'mechanism': 2, 'seed': seed} for seed in seeds)\n778:    relabeled = normalize_edges(permutation[edges])\n785:    key = episode['family'] + '_' + str(episode['seed'])\n786:    edge_key = 'Stanford3_edges' if episode['family'] == 'Stanford3' else key + '_edges'\n789:    assignment = data[key + '_z' + str(episode['mechanism'])]\n790:    noise = data[key + '_noise']\n791:    observed = data[key + '_y' + str(episode['mechanism'])]\n793:        covariates, assignment, noise = covariates[:64], assignment[:64], noise[:64]\n795:        observed = potential_outcome(assignment, covariates, noise, edges, episode['mechanism'])\n802:    return edges, covariates, assignment, observed, noise, permutation\n815:            cases.setdefault((episode['family'], episode['mechanism']), []).append(outcome)\n837:    for seed in dict.fromkeys(episode['seed'] for episode in episodes):\n838:        selected = [(episode, row) for episode, row in zip(episodes, outcomes) if episode['seed'] == seed]\n843:        records.append({'seed': int(seed), 'score': score, 'correct': all(row['ok'] and (episode['kind'] == 'scientific' or row['control'] == 1.) for episode, row in selected),\n845:                        'solution': {'cases': [{'family': episode['family'], 'mechanism': episode['mechanism'],\n876:    manifest, data = load_resources()\n877:    episodes = episode_plan(manifest, smoke)\n879:        expected = manifest['plan'][key]\n880:        actual = [episode['seed'] for episode in episode_plan(manifest, profile)]\n881:        if (any(type(seed) is not int for seed in expected) or expected != actual):\n908:        edges, covariates, assignment, observed, noise, permutation = episode_data(episode, data, smoke)\n983:        key = (episode['family'], episode['mechanism'], episode['seed'])\n986:            truth = float(np.mean(potential_outcome(np.ones(len(covariates)), covariates, noise, edges, episode['mechanism'])\n987:                                  - potential_outcome(np.zeros(len(covariates)), covariates, noise, edges, episode['mechanism'])))\n999:        solution = {'contrast': contrast, 'true_gate': truth, 'uncapped_error': uncapped_error,\n---\nname: generate-concept-figure\ndescription: Generate one reader-facing conceptual overview figure for paper generation as an editable draw.io diagram via the pinned Autoillustrate npm release, with a deterministic layout and an optional image-model restyle.\n---\n\n# Who runs this (important)\nDuring **paper generation the orchestrator owns this pipeline**: `src/scripts/paper.sh` and `paper_edit.sh` run the installed `autoillustrate` CLI synchronously as a post-draft step (`run_concept_figure_step`), derive every argument from `paper_strategy.json`, forward the selected outer agent, and promote the result to `./figures/<figure_id>.png`. The phase agents always run in a dedicated one-shot Docker container, even when the outer paper workflow is native; this limits them to the paper directory, selected-agent auth, and selected provider credentials. The paper-writing agent must **not** invoke this pipeline itself. The rest of this document describes the same CLI for standalone/manual use.\n\n# What the skill is about\nGenerate one reader-facing conceptual overview figure for the paper when a high-level glance-value visual will clarify the method, comparison story, or evidence structure. The figure is produced by the Autoillustrate pipeline (the `autoillustrate` npm release pinned in the agent image): each panel is a collision-checked, deterministically laid-out draw.io diagram, the panels are composed into a single editable `.drawio` file, and the composite is optionally restyled into a camera-ready PNG. The deliverable is a real `.drawio` source plus its export — only the final restyle pass touches a generative model.\n\n# When to use the skill\n- Final paper generation.\n- The paper needs an early conceptual figure that is easier to scan than a dense quantitative plot.\n- The grounded artifacts support a clean overview figure without inventing unsupported mechanisms or claims.\n- `paper_strategy.json` requests a required overview-style `diagram` figure or the paper prompt calls for an overview figure on page 1 or 2.\n- The figure is a methods/architecture/training-loop schematic with 1–3 structurally distinct panels. (For pure quantitative plots use matplotlib/seaborn instead.)\n\n# Prerequisites\nThe pipeline shells out to several tools. Confirm them before claiming a hard failure:\n- **`drawio` desktop CLI** on `PATH` (headless export). Without it Phases 2/4 cannot export.\n- **`autoillustrate` and `headless`** on `PATH`, plus the selected agent CLI (`claude`, `codex`, `cursor`, `gemini`, `opencode`, or `pi`).\n- For environment-authenticated OpenCode phase agents, set `PAPER_CONCEPT_FIGURE_AGENT_PROVIDER` to exactly one of `openai`, `gemini`, or `anthropic`; only that provider credential is forwarded.\n- **`OPENAI_API_KEY`** — the default VLM backend (`gpt-5.5`) for the Phase 3 per-panel inspection and the Phase 6 verification, and the image model (`gpt-image-2`) for the Phase 5 restyle. Without it those VLM calls and the restyle cannot run; you can still ship the deterministic Phase 4 export with `--skip-enhance`.\n- **`GEMINI_API_KEY`** — optional fallback. When OpenAI is unavailable, the paper orchestrator selects `nanobanana-pro`, `gemini-3.1-pro`, and `gemini-single` for enhancement and audits.\n- **A Python venv** with the toolkit deps. The container image bakes one and exposes its interpreter as `$VENV_PY`.\n\nBefore deciding a key is missing, check the active environment directly. OpenAI is the default; Gemini is the automatic fallback:\n```bash\npython - <<'PY'\nimport os\nfor k in (\"OPENAI_API_KEY\", \"GEMINI_API_KEY\"):\n    print(f\"{k}: {'available' if os.getenv(k) else 'missing'}\")\nPY\n```\nDo not claim a key is unavailable when the rendered paper prompt says it is expected to be available unless your direct check still shows it missing. Without an enhancement key, `--skip-enhance` still ships the deterministic Phase 4 export.\n\n# What to do\n1. Infer the central mechanism, comparison, or evidence story from grounded artifacts only. Decide whether one cohesive panel suffices or the content naturally splits into 2–3 structurally independent panels (e.g. *architecture · update rule · training loop*). Prefer one overview figure, not a full illustration suite.\n\n2. Confirm the installed CLI and selected agent are available:\n```bash\ncommand -v autoillustrate\nautoillustrate doctor --agent \"${AGENT:-claude}\"\n```\n\n3. In the project container, use the baked `$VENV_PY`. Native installations may let Autoillustrate create its cached venv or set `VENV_PY` explicitly.\n\n4. Run the pipeline against the manuscript. Resolve the strategy's exact figure id, pass `--output ./figures/<figure_id>.png`, forward the selected `--agent`, and provide a concise grounded prompt. Add `--skip-enhance` when no enhancement backend is available.\n\n**This pipeline can take ~1h** (it dispatches several selected-agent jobs and may run a VLM restyle). Run it **synchronously and block on it** — the caller must own the pipeline's full lifetime. Do **not** launch it as a background task that outlives the caller's turn (`run_in_background: true`, a trailing `&`, or a fire-and-forget agent step): when that turn ends the pipeline is orphaned and reaped mid-run, leaving the figure unrendered. In `paper.sh` and `paper_edit.sh` this is exactly what `run_concept_figure_step` does — a single synchronous invocation in the agent container, wrapped with `timeout` or Homebrew's `gtimeout` so a genuine hang is bounded. Native systems without either command skip this non-gating render step instead of launching an unbounded process. The pipeline writes `./figures/<figure_id>.png` (and `<figure_id>.prompts.json`) only on success; confirm those files exist before treating the figure as done.\n```bash\nautoillustrate ./paper.tex \\\n  --output ./figures/<figure_id>.png \\\n  --agent \"${AGENT:-claude}\" \\\n  --prompt \"Methods diagram that will be the main figure of this scientific research paper. <one or two sentences grounding the panels in the actual method>\"\n```\nThe orchestrator creates `runs/<YYYY-MM-DD-HHMMSS>/` in the working directory and writes the deliverables to `runs/<ts>/figures/`:\n- `full_figure.drawio` — editable draw.io source\n- `full_figure.png` — deterministic export (no model involved; always safe)\n- `full_figure_enhanced.png` — publication-grade restyle (only when Phase 5 ran)\n- `figure.json` — the validated 1–3 panel plan that drove the figure\n\nWith `--output` set, the pipeline also copies the best available figure (the enhanced export when Phase 5 ran, otherwise the deterministic export) to `./figures/<figure_id>.png` and drops the plan beside it as `./figures/<figure_id>.prompts.json`. The pipeline does not emit a PDF; the editable `full_figure.drawio` stays in the run workdir.\n\n5. Keep the visual style scientific and simple: clean diagrammatic composition, exact labels, no decorative clip-art, no unsupported architecture details, datasets, or numeric claims. When the paper contains multiple figures, keep colors logically consistent — reuse the same color for the same method/baseline/condition across figures.\n\n6. Confirm the promoted deliverable. With `--output` (step 4) the pipeline already wrote `./figures/<figure_id>.png` and `./figures/<figure_id>.prompts.json` — verify both exist. If you ran without `--output`, promote manually from the run workdir (enhanced export preferred, deterministic export as fallback):\n```bash\nRUN_FIGS=\"$(ls -td runs/*/figures | head -1)\"\nSRC_PNG=\"$RUN_FIGS/full_figure_enhanced.png\"; [[ -f \"$SRC_PNG\" ]] || SRC_PNG=\"$RUN_FIGS/full_figure.png\"\ncp \"$SRC_PNG\" \"./figures/<figure_id>.png\"\ncp \"$RUN_FIGS/figure.json\" \"./figures/<figure_id>.prompts.json\"   # the prompt/plan log\n```\nThe editable `full_figure.drawio` stays in the run workdir so the figure can be re-edited later. The pipeline produces no PDF; the manifest does not require one for this figure.\n\n7. When the strategy or prompt asks for a required overview/`diagram` figure, do not silently replace this workflow with a hand-drawn or purely matplotlib/TikZ schematic. Use this skill first unless it is impossible.\n\n8. If a prerequisite is missing (for example, no `drawio` CLI) or the pipeline fails, log an explicit skip/failure reason in both `./memory.md` and `./global_memory/memory.md` before falling back to another figure implementation. Apply the same fallback logging rule if the generated figure is too poor to use.\n\ntotal 20\ndrwx------ 3 agent agent 4096 Nov  7 03:30 .\ndrwx------ 8 agent agent 4096 Nov  7 03:30 ..\n-rw------- 1 agent agent    0 Nov  7 03:19 .broker.lock\n-r-------- 1 agent agent 1487 Nov  7 03:30 final_manifest.json\n-r-------- 1 agent agent  395 Nov  7 03:19 invocation.json\ndr-xr-xr-x 2 agent agent 4096 Nov  7 03:30 results\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
