{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_40","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"rg -n 'def baseline|own_treatment_ols|one_hop_ols|difference_in_means|design =|lstsq' task/evaluate_final.py | head -35; sed -n '580,636p' task/evaluate_final.py; rg -n 'p=.5|p=0.5|Bernoulli|bernoulli|randomization|cluster|assignment' task/task_contract.json | head -15; sed -n '70,90p' .codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/SKILL.md; jq '.grounding_sources[\\\"result.top_program_02\\\"]' paper_data.json\"","aggregated_output":"48:BASELINES = ('difference_in_means', 'own_treatment_ols', 'one_hop_ols', 'copy_observed', 'constant_prediction')\n378:            if method == 'difference_in_means':\n380:            design = np.column_stack((np.ones(count), covariates, assignment))\n381:            if method == 'one_hop_ols':\n386:                design = np.column_stack((design, exposure / np.maximum(degree, 1)))\n387:            coefficients = np.linalg.lstsq(design, outcome, rcond=None)[0]\n389:            if method == 'one_hop_ols':\n            except TimeoutError:\n                raise\n            except (RuntimeError, ValueError, OSError) as error:\n                self.broker_usable = False\n                raise BrokerTransportFailure(request.get('op', 'unknown')) from error\n            finally:\n                signal.setitimer(signal.ITIMER_REAL, 0)\n                signal.signal(signal.SIGALRM, previous)\n        else:\n            if request['op'] == 'reset':\n                self.close_channel()\n                self.channel = ProcessChannel('candidate', self.entrypoint, self.entrypoint.parent)\n            if self.channel is None:\n                raise ProtocolError('reset_required')\n            try:\n                result = self.channel.exchange(request, timeout)\n            except (TimeoutError, ProtocolError) as failure:\n                try:\n                    self.close_channel(failed=True)\n                except Exception:\n                    failure.add_note('secondary candidate cleanup failure')\n                raise\n        try:\n            bounded_json_line(result)\n        except (TypeError, ValueError, OverflowError, RecursionError):\n            raise ProtocolError('invalid_json_response') from None\n        return result\n\n    def close_channel(self, failed=False):\n        if self.channel is not None:\n            channel, self.channel = self.channel, None\n            channel.close(failed)\n\n    def close(self):\n        try:\n            self.close_channel()\n        finally:\n            if self.directory is not None:\n                self.directory.cleanup()\n\n\ndef run_declared_episodes(episodes, *, hard_deadline, finish_reserve, reset_timeout, episode_overhead,\n                          rpc_cap, clock, rpc, evaluate, worst_case, record_failure):\n    candidate_deadline = hard_deadline - finish_reserve\n    reset_slot = reset_timeout + episode_overhead\n    outcomes = [worst_case(episode) for episode in episodes]\n    if clock() + len(episodes) * reset_slot > candidate_deadline:\n        raise TimeoutError('insufficient time for declared reset reservations')\n    complete = True\n    for index, episode in enumerate(episodes):\n        episode_start = clock()\n        remaining = len(episodes) - index - 1\n        episode_deadline = candidate_deadline - remaining * reset_slot\n        work_deadline = episode_deadline - episode_overhead\n        current_operation = 'reset'\n        primary_failure = None\n\n9:    \"description\": \"Study when a fitted regression, evaluated at all-treated and all-control assignments, estimates finite-population GATE accurately. The candidate direction is ridge regression with an unpenalized intercept, own treatment, covariates, one-hop treated-neighbor fraction, fixed hinge bases and treatment-exposure interactions. Compare it with difference-in-means, own-treatment regression and linear one-hop regression. Test whether exposure adequacy, support near the endpoint interventions, interference strength and graph structure explain changes in bias and RMSE. Explicitly include misspecified two-hop interference, nonlinear interference and cluster assignment. This is a bounded simulation and semi-synthetic study, not a claim of universal superiority, identification under arbitrary interference, or novelty of regression adjustment itself. Favorable, unfavorable and inconclusive comparisons are all legitimate outcomes; publication requires uncertainty and limitations, not a positive effect. Search correctness means scientific-evaluation integrity and matched behavioral controls, not superiority. Final correctness independently means completed sealed integrity/control checks, not automatic publication. Fixed inputs, DGPs, score weights, finite penalties, explicit RPC operation counts and timing reservations are recorded in own-plane manifests. No feedback-dependence or changed-state gate applies to this nonadaptive regression task.\"\n1032:      \"Candidate receives only its current episode's topology, covariates, realized assignment and observed experimental outcomes, permitted prediction assignments and public fitting configuration. Search-visible artifacts must not embed concrete final seeds, final manifests, final-seed constants, final assets or seed-to-workload mappings.\",\n1048:      \"Evaluator-owned raw archive and normalized graph/example digests, source/row provenance, normalization rules fixed before splitting/features, randomization/generator seeds and nonoverlapping search/final split manifests. Show content-level cross-plane intersection checks, including different-ID duplicates and relabeling provenance. Record the Stanford3 supplied revision verification and applicable license/attribution; shared immutable code is not a held-out data violation.\",\n1057:      \"Low-level graph-cluster definition is deterministic balanced BFS over actual topology, not an optimized published design. M4 is length-two walk exposure including backtracking, not a unique-distance-two mean. Relabel-invariant multiset fingerprints conservatively reject possible graph overlap and raw row hashes exclude IDs. Frozen manifests document these scope limitations.\",\n```json\n{\n  \"claims\": [\n    {\n      \"claim\": \"text\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\"result.best_correct_score\"],\n      \"citation_keys\": [\"SomeKey2024\"]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n32. Run validator:\n```bash\npython scripts/validate_claims.py \\\n  --paper-data paper_data.json \\\n  --references references_provenance.json \\\n  --bib references.bib \\\n  --claims claims_grounding.json \\\n  --paper-dir .\n```\nThis validator also checks that `references.bib` and `references_provenance.json` stay in sync, and traces every `@evidence[[...]]` link under `--paper-dir` against the `scientific-evidence/` bundle via the `scientific-evidence` skill verifier. Every link must classify as `resolved` or `anchored`; any `dangling` link is a hard error you must fix before finalization. If paper text carries `@evidence[[...]]` tokens but the bundle is missing, generate it first with `bash ../scientific-evidence/scripts/scientific_evidence.sh emit-bundle --root-dir .`.\n{\n  \"attempt_id\": \"cycle01_endpoint_contrast_audit_attempt_01\",\n  \"id\": \"result.top_program_02\",\n  \"idea_id\": \"cycle01_endpoint_contrast_audit\",\n  \"program_dir\": \"work/results/t09/codex/20261107_014043/investigation/ideas/01_endpoint_contrast_audit_with_hidden_spillover_twins/program_1\",\n  \"program_id\": \"program_1\",\n  \"type\": \"metric\",\n  \"value\": 0.9909514004064053\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
